# Windsurf Rules — Astro Performance Starter

This project's canonical AI agent context lives in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) at the repo root. Windsurf reads `AGENTS.md` natively; this file is a Windsurf-specific overlay only.

Read `AGENTS.md` first. Everything below adds Windsurf-specific behaviour on top of it; nothing here repeats or overrides shared rules.

## Windsurf-specific directives

Every time you choose to apply a rule from `AGENTS.md`, explicitly state the rule in the output. You can abbreviate the rule description to a single word or phrase.

## Maintenance

Do not add shared project rules to this file. If a rule applies to all AI agents (Claude, Cursor, Codex, etc.), add it to the appropriate layer:

- Halt-on-violation rules → [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md)
- Engineering defaults → [`.claude/engineering.md`](.claude/engineering.md)
- Process and workflow → [`.claude/workflow.md`](.claude/workflow.md)
- Stack facts (versions, commands, budgets) → [`.claude/stack.md`](.claude/stack.md)

`AGENTS.md` is regenerated from those four files by `pnpm agents:build`; CI fails on drift. See [ADR-045](docs/adr/045-cross-tool-agents-spine.md) for the cross-tool spine rationale and [ADR-036](docs/adr/036-layered-constitution.md) for the layering rationale.
